> Plus, I'll just drop all my stuff on the Sokoban stairs and switch levels
> while I bless each individual item.  Encouraging players to perform
> tedious tasks because it's optimal goes the direction away from "fun".

You misunderstand.  What I mean is, your God/dess will not grant 
his/her blessing to every little thing you happen to be using.  
Go right ahead and bless things one at a time; the fourth or 
fifth time you dip something, you'll get some kind of "make up 
your mind what you want blessed, kid" message and the oldest 
blessing will end.   In terms of game design, I want the player 
to have to pick what to bless and what to leave uncursed, and 
then live with that decision. For a lot of characters, blessing 
things won't even be an option. 

